    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0315" n="203" xml:id="pg203"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4618: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                            notAfter="1919-06-04T02:54:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1919-06-02T16:00:00+05:31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received June 4, 1919, 2:54
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Following from [Harris at]
                    Novonikolaievsk.</p>
                <p>“249. June 2d, 4 p.m. Military conditions on Ufa front reported bad. Possible Ufa
                    may be evacuated soon.</p>
                <p>Stevens now Omsk. Situation on railway
                    between Kansk and Krasnoyarsk unchanged. Harris.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
